      book: 'Deuteronomy',
      chapter: 9,
      verse: 2,
      author: 'Tried By Fire',
      authorHandle: '@TriedByFire',
      profileImageUrl: undefined,
      text: `The city that they were promised to possess had some very powerful opponents in it who would not give the city over to the Israelites easily. It wasn’t as if Israel could just go in and ask, “Will you please give us this city and leave so that we can dwell here with our God?” No, there wouldn’t be a single person in their right mind that would just give up their home and land to strangers just because they were asked politely. Israel had no incentives, no leverage, and no strength to do anything about taking over this land. The fact of the matter is, they would have to heavily rely on the Lord’s provision and guidance if they were going to hold to the Lord’s promises. In Moses’ eyes, this was the moment that the Israelites were going to be tested the most as we see in the verses to follow.`,
