      book: 'Deuteronomy',
      chapter: 9,
      verse: 24,
      author: 'Tried By Fire',
      authorHandle: '@TriedByFire',
      profileImageUrl: undefined,
      text: `It’s been a difficult journey because of their own resistance to the Lord. We find, in this life, that when we resist the direction and will of God, we often make our lives harder and much less pleasurable. Looking back, Moses cannot think of a specific time when the children of Israel were just simply faithful to God. It was like pulling teeth with these people. God didn’t waste these years of wandering. He used them to correct and build His people. They needed a change of heart and mind, and the only way to do that was to get them to wander. Even still, it took them the better part of 39 years to finally get to trusting in the Lord...`,
