      author: 'Tried By Fire',
      authorHandle: '@TriedByFire',
      profileImageUrl: undefined,
      text: `God judges sin. Moses was in constant prayer and intercession with God for the sake of the people. Moses was the “mediator” (so to speak) at this particular juncture. He couldn’t do anything but plead with the Lord on their behalf, and the Lord listened and accepted Moses’ faith, but He also taught the children through very complex and difficult trials because of their lack of faith. The real treasure here is to hear how faith-filled Moses’ prayer was for the people. You can see the heart of a man through the way he prays for others.`,
