      chapter: 9,
      verse: 29,
      author: 'Tried By Fire',
      authorHandle: '@TriedByFire',
      profileImageUrl: undefined,
      text: `We know we DESERVE God’s wrath. We deserve God’s judgement. We deserve damnation and hell. But Jesus Christ gave us an escape from that. His death and burial were a symbol of God’s grace for us, and His resurrection was a symbol of God’s providence for anyone that would be willing to believe in Him. The children of Israel needed that same faith. They needed to know they deserved God’s wrath, but if they had faith in God, they wouldn’t receive it. God would provide mercy rather than wrath because His people would turn to Him and seek Him out. Deuteronomy 10 Bible Stories sections: V. 1-11, 12-22.`,
