      book: 'Deuteronomy',
      chapter: 9,
      verse: 5,
      author: 'Tried By Fire',
      authorHandle: '@TriedByFire',
      profileImageUrl: undefined,
      text: `We have to understand that (though we have a will), God’s Will will always triumph over man’s will! The comforting fact, for us (the saved), is that we can depend on God’s Will to always be right and good, even if it doesn’t look like it from our eyes. We need to trust in the Lord’s deliverance based on His promises, not based on our goodness. We cannot think we have the strength to do anything simply because we have the Lord. I know many people who misquote this verse from Philippians… "I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me." Philippians 4:13`,
      likes: 0,
