      id: 'deuteronomy_9_5_para4',
      book: 'Deuteronomy',
      chapter: 9,
      verse: 5,
      author: 'Tried By Fire',
      authorHandle: '@TriedByFire',
      profileImageUrl: undefined,
      text: `You cannot do “all things” simply because Christ strengthens you. Rather, you can do all of the things of Christ because He strengthens you. It must be CHRIST’S ordinance and Will in order for us to get our strength to do it. The Israelites needed to rely on God in this matter, and they needed to get rid of the idea that their righteousness is what ultimately gets them their victory. The victory is not in us, it’s in Jesus alone. We are not righteous in anything we do, it is only Christ who is righteous, and so it is only Christ we must trust in. "As it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one: There is none that understandeth, there is none that seeketh after God. They are all gone out of the way, they are together become unprofitable; there is none that doeth good, no, not one." Romans 3:10-12`,
