      author: 'Tried By Fire',
      authorHandle: '@TriedByFire',
      profileImageUrl: undefined,
      text: `Moses may seem a little rude here by calling them “stiffnecked” or “prideful,” but Moses doesn’t just leave them with name-calling. Moses will now prove how they were stiffnecked. Honestly, the only one that could rightly evaluate these people would be Moses, because Moses had to LEAD them this entire time, and they were a difficult bunch to get to listen. BUT, so was Moses. God chose Moses to talk to Pharaoh at the beginning of all of this, and Moses rejected it over and over again, so that it would be Aaron that would do the talking... That’s a conversation for a different study. Moses displays some of the ways that the people proved their pride in the past...`,
